        "say": [
          "Single-table design collapses relational entities into a unified NoSQL key space, eliminating expensive multi-table joins and delivering predictable single-digit millisecond latency at any scale.",
          "Overloading generic partition keys (`PK`) and sort keys (`SK`) enables diverse entity hierarchies to reside seamlessly within the same physical storage partitions.",
          "In relational databases like PostgreSQL or MySQL, modeling one-to-many and many-to-many relationships involves creating dozens of normalized tables connected by foreign keys and relational SQL JOIN queries.",
          "In massive-scale distributed NoSQL systems like Amazon DynamoDB, relational JOIN queries do not exist: a relational query joining five tables would require scattered cross-partition network RPCs that destroy predictable single-digit millisecond latency.",
          "Amazon DynamoDB achieves predictable O(1) read and write latency at petabyte scale through Single-Table Design: modeling all application entities (Users, Orders, Products, Payments) within a single unified DynamoDB table.",
          "Single-Table Design relies on generic primary keys: a Partition Key (`PK`) and a Sort Key (`SK`), typically stored as composite strings (e.g. `PK = USER#101`, `SK = PROFILE` or `SK = ORDER#2026-11-12`).",
          "By co-locating related parent and child entities within the exact same partition key (`PK = USER#101`), an application can fetch a user profile and all their recent orders in a single, lightning-fast `Query` API call with zero JOIN overhead!",
          "Analyze the mathematical data co-location model comparing relational multi-table JOINs with DynamoDB single-table partitions below."
        ],
